{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/rafttest/interaction_env_handler_add_nodes.go | sed -n '140,177p'; grep -R -n '\\\\.History =\\\\|History:' ../agent-source/rafttest --include='*.go'; nl -ba ../agent-source/raft.go | sed -n '769,773p;1189,1202p'\"","aggregated_output":"   769\tfunc (r *raft) appliedSnap(snap *pb.Snapshot) {\n   770\t\tindex := snap.Metadata.Index\n   771\t\tr.raftLog.stableSnapTo(index)\n   772\t\tr.appliedTo(index, 0 /* size */)\n   773\t}\n  1189\t\tcase pb.MsgStorageAppendResp:\n  1190\t\t\tif m.Index != 0 {\n  1191\t\t\t\tr.raftLog.stableTo(entryID{term: m.LogTerm, index: m.Index})\n  1192\t\t\t}\n  1193\t\t\tif m.Snapshot != nil {\n  1194\t\t\t\tr.appliedSnap(m.Snapshot)\n  1195\t\t\t}\n  1196\t\n  1197\t\tcase pb.MsgStorageApplyResp:\n  1198\t\t\tif len(m.Entries) > 0 {\n  1199\t\t\t\tindex := m.Entries[len(m.Entries)-1].Index\n  1200\t\t\t\tr.appliedTo(index, entsSize(m.Entries))\n  1201\t\t\t\tr.reduceUncommittedSize(payloadsSize(m.Entries))\n  1202\t\t\t}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The snapshot adapter has a concrete observation gap: received snapshots update MemoryStorage, but its exported Snapshot method returns the separate application History. In the paths read, History changes at bootstrap and entry application, not when a snapshot is received. I’ll retain this as a harness limitation to resolve before using the adapter as an oracle for snapshot recovery.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\nfor i,f,a,b in [('n-interaction-owner','rafttest/interaction_env.go',27,102),('n-interaction-bootstrap','rafttest/interaction_env_handler_add_nodes.go',92,163),('n-interaction-send-snapshot','rafttest/interaction_env_handler_send_snapshot.go',33,50),('n-rafttest-node-loop','rafttest/node.go',65,117)]:sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind='code_observation'))\ns=dict(action='research',rationale='Retain a newly sourced snapshot-observation limitation in the in-repository driver and a precise remaining cross-stream responsibility question; this is not protocol defect attribution.',sources=sources,feedback=dict(ref_ids=[x['id'] for x in sources]+['n-interaction-append','n-interaction-apply','src-async-contract','s-log-delivery','src-term-dispatch','src-append-reset'],answered='InteractionEnv owns separate AppendWork, ApplyWork and application History. Its storage wrapper returns the latest History snapshot, rather than the embedded MemoryStorage snapshot. AddNodes initializes History from the bootstrap snapshot; the read processApply path extends History using prior History data and the applied entry. The inspected received-snapshot append path calls Storage.ApplySnapshot and returns without updating History. A search of History assignments in rafttest found initialization and entry-application append only. Thus received snapshot storage and the adapter-exported application snapshot can diverge; subsequent Snapshot/SendSnapshot observations through this adapter are not automatically an oracle for correctly reconstructed application state. This is an adapter observation limitation, not a demonstrated failure of raft.restore. Separately, the simple rafttest Node loop appends storage and advances while omitting committed-entry application; it is likewise unsuitable as a driver for a membership/application responsibility without completing those duties. At the implementation boundary, async MsgStorageAppendResp carrying a snapshot invokes appliedSnap and advances applied bookkeeping, while MsgStorageApplyResp records entry completion. The contract permits different storage targets to process in either order. nextCommittedEnts prevents new delivery while a snapshot is pending, but that does not by itself explain the treatment of older ApplyWork already handed to the caller.',remaining=['Snapshot cross-stream history: determine who orders or suppresses previously issued entry application relative to a later snapshot installation, given independent append/apply targets; inspect snapshot installation duties before deriving any obligation.','Before reusing InteractionEnv for such a check, either establish how received snapshot state reaches History or build an explicit application owner that models it correctly. Do not substitute the stale History snapshot as implementation output.','No producer-correlated async snapshot/application execution has been constructed, and no result transfers from the two synchronous accepted checks.'],understanding='updated',rationale='This smaller source step identifies the exact adapter state split and the unresolved older-work premise. A test using the existing adapter unchanged could manufacture an application-state discrepancy, so construction must first distinguish the caller-owned snapshot application from raft bookkeeping.'))\nopen('submission.json','w').write(json.dumps(s,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-02_22-35-07-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
